---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const RELEASES = 'https://github.com/singularityos-lab/os/releases';
---

<Base title="Download - Singularity OS">
  <section class="hero">
    <h1>Try it on your machine.</h1>
    <p class="lede">Singularity ships as part of Sinty OS. Pick the image for your computer, write it to a USB stick, and install.</p>
    <div class="cta">
      <a class="btn btn-solid" href={`${RELEASES}/tag/nightly`}>Download for PC</a>
      <a class="btn" href={`${RELEASES}/tag/nightly-arm64`}>Download for ARM</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="image">
    <h2 class="section-title">Pick your image</h2>
    <div class="grid">
      <a class="cell" href={`${RELEASES}/tag/nightly`}><span class="k">x86_64</span><h3>PC</h3><p>Desktops and laptops with a 64-bit Intel or AMD processor. Intel, AMD and NVIDIA graphics.</p></a>
      <a class="cell" href={`${RELEASES}/tag/nightly-arm64`}><span class="k">aarch64</span><h3>ARM</h3><p>Jetson, Rockchip RK3588, Raspberry Pi 4 and 5, Snapdragon laptops and virtual machines. Boards without a TPM unlock with a passphrase.</p></a>
      <a class="cell" href="/docs/os/install/"><span class="k">Guide</span><h3>Installing</h3><p>Write the image with Drive Writer or dd, start from the stick, and follow the installer.</p></a>
      <a class="cell" href="/docs/os/arm/"><span class="k">ARM</span><h3>Boards and firmware</h3><p>Which boards are supported, which firmware they need, and how the kernel is chosen.</p></a>
      <a class="cell" href="/docs/os/requirements/"><span class="k">Requirements</span><h3>What you need</h3><p>UEFI firmware, a TPM 2.0 on PC, a few GB of memory and an SSD.</p></a>
      <a class="cell" href="/docs/getting-started"><span class="k">Developers</span><h3>From source</h3><p>Build the desktop with meson on the system you already have.</p></a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
